  "question": {
    "text": "On complete combustion 1.0 g of an organic compound (X) gave 1.46 g of \\(\\mathrm{CO}_2\\) and 0.567 g of \\(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\). The empirical formula mass of compound \\((\\mathrm{X})\\) is ________ g.<br />(Given molar mass in \\(\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{C}: 12, \\mathrm{H}: 1, \\mathrm{O}: 16\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "46t4l",
      "text": "30",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mGaJ0",
      "text": "45",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "V0DCb",
      "text": "60",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gqXRj",
      "text": "15",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Moles of ' C ' \\(=\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{CO}_2}=\\frac{1.46}{44}=0.033\\)<br />Moles of ' C ' \\(=\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{C}}=0.033 \\times 12\\)<br />Moles of 'H' \\(=2 \\times \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}=2 \\times \\frac{0.567}{18}=0.063\\)<br />Mass of ' H ' \\(=0.0063\\)<br />Mass of Oxygen \\((\\mathrm{O})=1-\\left(\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{c}}+\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{H}}\\right)\\) \\(=1-(0.033 \\times 12+0.063 \\times 1)=0.541 \\mathrm{gm}\\)<br />Moles of ' O ' \\(=\\frac{0.541}{16}=0.033\\)<br />Empirical formula \\(=\\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\)<br />Empirical formula mass \\(=30\\).",
    "image": null
  },
